body:
FEATURE SPEC: Scorecard Progressive Disclosure
Based on T24 (Khan Academy critique) + ADHD design principle: one signal at a time

Filed by: GD
For: GA implementation in exam.html

WHY
Current scorecard: hero score + grade + coach message + standards grid all render simultaneously.
For ADHD: Kai processes the big number, then immediately gets a grid of per-standard scores
while still absorbing the headline. Too much at once.

T24 critique of KA: they surface score + 8+ skill bars in one view. Same failure pattern.

DESIGN GOAL: Let the number land. Then reveal the breakdown on demand.

CURRENT SCORECARD ORDER
1. Score big (count-up animation) -- correct, keep
2. Grade letter -- correct, keep
3. Coach message -- correct, keep
4. "Your Game Plan" heading + standards-grid -- TOO IMMEDIATE. Should be deferred.
5. CTA -- correct, keep after Game Plan

REDESIGN: TWO PHASES

PHASE 1 (score reveal -- what shows immediately)
  - Score big (count-up)
  - Grade letter
  - Coach message (12 words max, MCM voice)
  - CTA: "See Your Game Plan" button (replaces standards grid)
  - No standards grid visible

PHASE 2 (on demand -- after button press)
  - Button text changes to "Game Plan ✓"
  - standards-grid slides in below (CSS max-height transition or simple display:block)
  - "Your Game Plan" heading becomes visible
  - CTA (Run It Back / Dashboard) moves to BELOW the grid

COGNITIVE RATIONALE (ADHD)
- Phase 1: 1 number, 1 grade, 1 sentence. Enough to feel the result.
- Phase 2: Standards detail when Kai CHOOSES to see it. Not pushed on him.
- Button is the decision gate. Kai controls when he's ready for breakdown.

IMPLEMENTATION

HTML structure change in buildScorecard():
  Replace this block (current):
    html += '<h3>Your Game Plan</h3>';
    html += '<div class="standards-grid">...</div>';
    [CTA block]

  With:
    html += '<button id="gameplanBtn" class="btn-secondary" onclick="revealGamePlan()">📋 See Your Game Plan</button>';
    html += '<div id="gamePlanSection" style="display:none;">';
    html += '<h3>Your Game Plan</h3>';
    html += '<div class="standards-grid">...</div>';
    html += '</div>';
    [CTA block] -- leave in same position BELOW the game plan section

JS: add revealGamePlan() function
  function revealGamePlan() {
    document.getElementById('gamePlanSection').style.display = '';
    var btn = document.getElementById('gameplanBtn');
    btn.textContent = '📋 Game Plan ✓';
    btn.disabled = true;
    btn.style.opacity = '0.5';
    btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
  }

CSS additions (exam.html inline style block):
  #gamePlanSection {
    animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease;
  }
  @keyframes fadeIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #gamePlanSection { animation: none; }
  }

  #gameplanBtn {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  #gameplanBtn[disabled] {
    cursor: default;
  }

EDGE CASES
- No standards data (all questions untagged): standards-grid is empty. Keep button but show
  "No breakdown available" inside gamePlanSection instead of empty grid.
- Single standard: game plan button still shows. Even for 1 standard, the disclosure is valid.
- Retake / Run It Back flow: gamePlanSection resets on reload (location.reload()), so no state issue.

ACCEPT CRITERIA
[x] On score reveal: only score, grade, coach message, and "See Your Game Plan" button are visible
[x] Standards grid is hidden until button pressed
[x] Button press reveals grid with subtle fade-in (or instant, if reduced-motion)
[x] Button becomes disabled/checked after reveal (cannot toggle closed)
[x] Aria: button has aria-pressed=false initially, true after reveal
[x] CTA (Run It Back / Dashboard) remains below game plan (after the grid)
[x] No change to score count-up animation
